  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Acidity is directly proportional to conjugated base stability.<br /><img alt=\"\" height=\"182\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EM0010392_AnsExp1_2.jpg\" width=\"444\" /><br /><img alt=\"\" height=\"172\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EM0010392_AnsExp1_1.jpg\" width=\"469\" /><br /><br />Stability order of conjugate bases is III &gt; I &gt; II &gt; IV<br /><br />Conjugate base in I is stabilised by - I &gt; + M<br /><br /><span style=\"font-size: 12.7272720336914px; line-height: 20.8000011444092px;\">Conjugate&nbsp;</span>base in II is destabilised by + I and hyperconjugation.<br /><br /><span style=\"font-size: 12.7272720336914px; line-height: 20.8000011444092px;\">Conjugate</span><span style=\"font-size: 12.7272720336914px; line-height: 20.8000011444092px;\">&nbsp;</span> base in III is stabilised by strong withdrawing effect of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> by - I &amp; - M effect.<br /><br /><span style=\"font-size: 12.7272720336914px; line-height: 20.8000011444092px;\">Conjugate&nbsp;</span>base in IV is destabilised by + M effect of<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>OCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>acidic</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>character</mi><mtext>&#8201;&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#8733;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#8733;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>HC</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></math><br /><br />Electron releasing group (i.e +I effect, +M) decreases the acidic strength&nbsp;<br />Electron withdrawing group (i.e -I effect,-M) increases acidic strength.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5386402e-e2b5-4ca8-b3d2-85df6bf58969-38.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 160px;\" /><br />&nbsp;",
